    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "LIAM REILLY AUCTIONEERS are thrilled to present this immaculate 3 Bedroom Semi-Detached Bungalow to the market.\n\nA superb opportunity to acquire an exceptionally well-presented three-bedroom semi-detached bungalow in the mature and highly convenient Beechdale development in Dunboyne.\n\n211 Beechdale comes to the market in pristine condition throughout and is, in our opinion, one of the finest properties of its type to come to the market in Dunboyne in recent times.\n\nThe present owners have clearly taken great pride in the property, with the accommodation beautifully maintained and thoughtfully upgraded to create a stylish, comfortable and highly practical home. From the moment you arrive, the attention to detail is immediately apparent, with an attractive red-brick façade, private driveway and carefully maintained planting creating an excellent first impression.\n\nInternally, the property is presented in excellent decorative order throughout. A particularly impressive feature is the spacious kitchen/dining area, which forms the heart of the home. Finished with an extensive range of contemporary fitted units, generous worktop space, tiled flooring, integrated cooking appliances and excellent storage, there is ample room for a full-size dining table, making this a wonderful everyday living and entertaining space.\n\nThe living room is equally inviting, tastefully decorated in soft neutral tones and featuring an attractive period-style fireplace with decorative tiled inset and stove, together with plantation-style window shutters which feature extensively throughout the property.\n\nThere are three bedrooms, all presented to the same excellent standard. The principal bedroom benefits from excellent storage together with access to a beautifully finished shower room. The remaining bedrooms provide flexible accommodation suitable for family use, guests or a home office.\n\nThere are two bathrooms/shower rooms, both finished to a high standard with contemporary sanitary ware and attractive tiling.\n\nOutside, the rear garden has been exceptionally well cared for and provides a delightful private outdoor space. It incorporates a neat lawn bordered by mature planting together with a raised decked seating area, ideal for outdoor dining and entertaining. A useful, detached garden building provides additional storage and utility space.\n\nTo the front, a private driveway provides convenient off-street parking.\n\nThe combination of its single-storey accommodation, immaculate condition, three-bedroom layout and mature Dunboyne setting should ensure that 211 Beechdale will appeal to a wide variety of purchasers, including families, first-time buyers, those trading down from a larger home and purchasers seeking comfortable accommodation without the need for further expenditure.\nThis is quite simply a property that must be viewed to be fully appreciated.\n\nAccommodation\nThe accommodation briefly comprises:\nEntrance Hall\nBright and welcoming entrance hallway with tiled flooring and access to the principal accommodation.\n\nLiving Room\nA beautifully presented reception room featuring an attractive period-style fireplace with decorative tiled inset and stove, neutral décor, contemporary flooring and plantation-style window shutters.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room\nA particularly impressive and generously proportioned room fitted with an extensive range of contemporary wall and floor units, generous worktop space, tiled flooring, integrated oven and hob, extractor fan and ample space for a substantial dining table. Double doors provide direct access to the rear garden and decked area.\n\nBedroom 1\nGenerous double bedroom beautifully presented with plantation-style shutters, excellent storage and access to shower room facilities.\n\nBedroom 2\nWell-proportioned double bedroom with extensive fitted wardrobes and plantation-style shutters.\n\nBedroom 3\nA comfortable bedroom suitable for use as a child's bedroom, guest room or home office.\n\nBathrooms / Shower Rooms\nTwo well-appointed shower/bathroom facilities finished with contemporary tiling and sanitary ware.\n\nOutside\nPrivate driveway to the front providing off-street parking. To the rear is a beautifully maintained enclosed garden with lawn, mature planting and an attractive raised decked area providing an excellent outdoor entertaining space. Detached garden building providing useful additional storage/utility accommodation.\n\nLocation\nBeechdale is a mature residential development conveniently positioned in Dunboyne, one of Co. Meath's most popular and well-established commuter towns. Dunboyne offers an excellent range of everyday amenities including shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, sporting facilities and both primary and secondary schools.\n\nThe town is particularly well connected for commuters, with Dunboyne Train Station providing rail services on the DublinMaynooth/Longford/M3 Parkway route, while the nearby M3/N3 road network provides convenient access towards Blanchardstown, the M50 and Dublin City. The combination of a mature residential setting and excellent transport and local amenities makes Dunboyne an extremely convenient location for family living.\n\nFeatures\n•Superb 3 bedroom semi-detached bungalow\n•Presented in pristine condition throughout\n•Two bathrooms / shower rooms\n•Impressive modern kitchen and dining area\n•Attractive living room with feature fireplace and stove\n•Plantation-style window shutters\n•Extensive fitted storage\n•Excellent decorative condition\n•Private off-street parking\n•Beautifully maintained rear garden\n•Raised decked entertaining area\n•Useful detached garden building\n•Mature and highly convenient residential location\n•Excellent access to Dunboyne Village and local amenities\n•Convenient to rail and M3/N3 transport links\n•BER: C\n\nViewing\nViewing is highly recommended and strictly by appointment through the sole selling agents Liam Reilly Auctioneers.\n\nLIAM REILLY AUCTIONEERS give notice that; All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for the use and occupation, and other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them.\n\n\n"
      },
